sentences.l:
And of them, as much as from the ships, from the wall, the ditch shut in,
was full alike of horses and of men, shield-bearers,
pressed together;

both to the huts of Ajax, Telamon’s-son,
and to Achilles’, who at the farthest the well-balanced ships
had drawn up, trusting in manliness and in strength of hands;

and after them Idomeneus and Idomeneus’ follower,
Meriones, the equal of Enyalius, killer of men,
and after them Eurypylus, Euaemon’s splendid son;
